#!spectest
# mode: run
# adjudicator: ggdef
# since: spec-v0.1
# features: [equality, traits, enum]
# doc: |
#   THE PARENLESS VARIANT PATH — the shape that caught a SILENT ACCEPT in D46's
#   own gate, and the one cell the rest of the corpus does not reach.
#
#   `Direction.North` without parentheses is a legal nullary-variant
#   construction (the Book teaches both spellings), but it leaves `unify` with
#   an inference-poisoned result type. A gate that judges only the UNIFIED type
#   therefore reads "no opinion", accepts, and the comparison answers address
#   identity — while `d == e` on the SAME enum, one line away, is refused. The
#   defect is position-dependent, which is what makes it invisible: every other
#   reject seed in this corpus stays red under it.
#
#   So the gate judges the OPERANDS whenever the unified type carries no verdict.
#   Revert that fallback and this seed goes green while all the others stay red;
#   it is the only witness for that arm. Do not let it be "covered" by a
#   parenthesised sibling — the parentheses are the whole variable.
# expect:
#   exit: 1
#   stdout: ""
#   reject: E_UnsupportedOperator
#!end

enum Direction:
    North
    South

void main():
    Direction d = Direction.North
    bool a = d == Direction.North
    print(f"{a}")
